{
  "id": "minimum-cost-to-connect-sticks",
  "questionId": "minimum-cost-to-connect-sticks",
  "slug": "minimum-cost-to-connect-sticks",
  "title": "Minimum Cost to Connect Sticks",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Heap",
  "patterns": [
    "heap",
    "min-heap",
    "greedy"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "connecting a small stick early keeps its length contributing to fewer future combination costs; connecting two large sticks early makes that big sum get added again and again in later combinations",
    "so at every step, the cheapest move is to combine whichever two sticks are currently smallest",
    "a heap gives fast repeated access to the two smallest values without re-sorting the whole collection each time",
    "push all stick lengths onto a min-heap. repeatedly pop the two smallest, add their sum to a running total cost, and push the sum back onto the heap. stop when only one stick remains"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "re-sorting the entire array after every single combination instead of using a heap, which is much slower",
    "combining the two largest sticks first instead of the two smallest, producing a higher total cost",
    "forgetting to push the newly combined stick back into the heap before continuing"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have a collection of `sticks`, each with a positive length, and you\nwant to combine them all into a single stick. Each move, you may pick any\ntwo sticks and connect them, which costs an amount equal to the sum of\ntheir two lengths; the resulting combined stick is then added back to\nyour collection, replacing the two you used, and you repeat until only\none stick remains.\n\n**Return the minimum total cost to combine everything into one stick.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= sticks.length <= 10000",
      "1 <= sticks[i] <= 100000"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "only one stick, requiring zero cost",
      "exactly two sticks",
      "all sticks the same length",
      "many sticks of length 1"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "sticks = [2, 4, 3]",
        "output": "14",
        "expectedOutput": "14",
        "explanation": "connect 2 and 3 first for a cost of 5, producing a stick of length 5; then connect 5 and 4 for a cost of 9; total cost is 5 + 9 = 14"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "sticks = [1, 8, 3, 5]",
        "output": "30",
        "expectedOutput": "30",
        "explanation": "connect 1 and 3 (cost 4, producing 4); connect 4 and 5 (cost 9, producing 9); connect 9 and 8 (cost 17); total is 4 + 9 + 17 = 30"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "sticks = [1]",
        "output": "0",
        "expectedOutput": "0",
        "explanation": "a single stick needs no connecting at all"
      }
